# Comparación real: 24 escenarios F-01

Comparación emparejada por ID con el mismo modelo `gpt-5.4-mini`, dataset `development`, semilla 42, modo `end-to-end` y una repetición por estrategia. Single-pass: `.eval-results/f01-24-20261115T084506Z/`; multipass: `.eval-results/f02-24-20261115-multipass/`. Los informes locales están ignorados por Git. Multipass usa `multipass-openai-4` y los cambios de trabajo no confirmados de esta rama.

| Resultado automático | Single-pass | Multipass |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| PASS | 23 | 2 |
| FAIL | 1 | 22 |
| Intentos de proveedor | 54 | 139 |
| Mayor número de intentos en un lote | 8 | 12 |

Los 24 IDs coinciden. La cota es de 18 intentos por lote; multipass se repartió en 16 lotes, con preflight máximo de 216 intentos incluyendo posibles borradores y correcciones. Los cambios de lote no modifican la selección ni el historial de cada caso. No se midieron tokens ni coste.

En multipass, 17 fallos informan que la interpretación requiere revisión humana y 5 indican que no superó la validación. Son resultados del evaluador de extremo a extremo: una abstención segura puede ser apropiada, pero este runner la presenta como error y no entrega hechos ni acción. No se puede asumir que cada fallo sea una extracción semántica incorrecta. Single-pass y multipass fallaron ambos `F01D1-trust_real-P1-V2`; los otros 21 FAIL de multipass eran PASS automáticos de single-pass.

## Hallazgo manual: falso PASS

`F01D1-time_nonurgent-P2-V2` fue PASS automático en ambas estrategias, pero multipass interpretó una preferencia de esperar doce meses o más como `OPT_OUT` y produjo `STOP_CONTACT`. El mensaje no solicita dejar de recibir comunicaciones. Los checks de este caso no prohíben `OPT_OUT` y `expectedAction` es `null`, por lo que el veredicto automático no detecta el problema. El mismo resultado de multipass atribuyó `desired_locations = Madrid` a una ciudad de referencia, sin que el mensaje establezca expresamente que sea la ubicación buscada. Estos hallazgos son revisión manual, no cambios retroactivos al oráculo ni una nueva puntuación automática.

El otro PASS multipass fue `F01D1-trust_real-P2-V2` con `HANDOFF`. No se ha revisado manualmente cada salida de los 24 casos. El caso de opt-out real B10 no completó la interpretación multipass, por lo que no demuestra que esa protección se haya gestionado correctamente; debe revisarse por separado antes de modificar guardas.

Las anotaciones del dataset están auditadas internamente y pendientes de revisión independiente. Una repetición por estrategia y un subconjunto correlacionado no permiten establecer fiabilidad general ni un ganador estadístico. Las métricas comparan checks provisionales y disponibilidad de resultados, no la calidad semántica de todos los casos.
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';
import type { Interpreter, SubjectRef } from '../../../contracts';
import { validateInterpretation, failure } from '../validation';
import { runPipeline } from './pipeline';
import type { FakeTransport } from './scheduler';
import { PROMPT_VERSION } from './prompts';
import { validateAssertions } from '../../../domain/facts';
import type { GroupingCounts, OperationTrace, ReviewCounts } from './trace';

export type MultipassDiagnostic = {
  finalStatus: 'consolidated' | 'human_review_required' | 'failed';
  failureCode: string | null;
  consumed: number;
  operations: Pick<OperationTrace, 'role' | 'status' | 'durationMs' | 'cause'>[];
  reviewCounts?: ReviewCounts;
  groupingCounts?: GroupingCounts;
  reviewReasonCategories?: string[];
  reviewDetails?: unknown;
};

// Versioned PoC profile: sensitive financial amounts and purchase structure
// require corroboration. Sensitivity is not used as a proxy for materiality.
export const RECONCILIATION_PROFILE = { version: 'poc-material-1', fields: ['declared_monthly_income', 'available_savings', 'monthly_debt', 'buyer_count'] } as const;
export class MultipassInterpreter implements Interpreter {
  constructor(private transport: FakeTransport, private onDiagnostic?: (diagnostic: MultipassDiagnostic) => void, private captureReviewDetails = false) {}
  async interpret(input: Parameters<Interpreter['interpret']>[0]) {
    const historical = input.caseSnapshot.assertions;
    // Case identity is intrinsic to the case. Other identities only come from
    // existing, non-rejected case assertions; no participants are invented.
    const subjects: SubjectRef[] = [{ scope: 'case', id: input.caseSnapshot.caseId }];
    for (const assertion of historical) if (assertion.reviewStatus !== 'rejected' && validateAssertions([assertion], input.messages, input.factSchema).ok && !subjects.some(s => s.scope === assertion.subjectRef.scope && s.id === assertion.subjectRef.id)) subjects.push(assertion.subjectRef);
    const snapshot = { caseId: input.caseSnapshot.caseId, messages: input.messages, factSchema: input.factSchema, agentProfile: input.agentProfile, knownSubjects: subjects, historicalAssertions: historical, historicalBlockers: input.caseSnapshot.blockers, materialFieldIds: RECONCILIATION_PROFILE.fields.filter(id => input.factSchema.fields.some(f => f.id === id)) };
    try {
      const { result, trace, attributionDiagnostics } = await runPipeline({ runId: randomUUID(), snapshot, transport: this.transport, instructionVersion: PROMPT_VERSION, locateSpans: true });
      try {
        const reviewReasonCategories = result.status === 'human_review_required' ? [...new Set(result.reasons.map(reason => reason.startsWith('Grouping ') ? 'grouping' : reason.startsWith('Subject attribution') ? 'subject_attribution' : reason.startsWith('Conflicting contextual') ? 'conflicting_reviews' : reason.startsWith('Protected ') || reason.startsWith('Adjudication conflicts') ? 'protected_safety' : reason.startsWith('Ambiguous ') ? 'ambiguous_identity' : reason.startsWith('Unresolved:') ? 'unresolved_material' : 'other'))] : undefined;
        this.onDiagnostic?.({ finalStatus: result.status, failureCode: result.status === 'failed' ? result.code : null, consumed: trace.consumed, operations: trace.operations.map(({ role, status, durationMs, cause }) => ({ role, status, durationMs, ...(cause && { cause }) })), ...(trace.reviewCounts && { reviewCounts: trace.reviewCounts }), ...(trace.groupingCounts && { groupingCounts: trace.groupingCounts }), ...(reviewReasonCategories && { reviewReasonCategories }), ...(this.captureReviewDetails && result.status === 'human_review_required' && { reviewDetails: { reasons: result.reasons, disputes: result.disputes, safetyFindings: result.safetyFindings, attributionDiagnostics } }) });
      } catch { /* Diagnostics must not alter interpretation. */ }
      if (result.status === 'human_review_required') return failure('MODEL_OUTPUT_INVALID', 'La interpretación requiere revisión humana');
      if (result.status === 'failed') {
        const provider = trace.operations.some(o => ['error', 'timeout', 'cancelled'].includes(o.status));
        return failure(provider ? 'MODEL_UNAVAILABLE' : 'MODEL_OUTPUT_INVALID', provider ? 'No se pudo completar la interpretación' : 'La interpretación no superó la validación', provider);
      }
      return validateInterpretation(result.interpretation, input);
    } catch { return failure('MODEL_UNAVAILABLE', 'No se pudo completar la interpretación', true); }
  }
}
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import type { FactAssertion, Message, SubjectRef } from '../../../contracts';
import type { ClaimGroup, ContextReview } from './contracts';
import { validateOccurrence } from './evidence';
import { sameEvidence } from './safety';

/** S2 supplies semantic classification; this stage verifies its provenance and
 * consistency. Canonical IDs are pseudonymous references, not authentication. */
export function bindSubjects(input: { groups: ClaimGroup[]; reviews: ContextReview[]; messages: Message[]; historicalAssertions: FactAssertion[]; knownSubjects: SubjectRef[]; caseId: string; diagnostics: { candidateId: string; code: string }[] }) {
  const { groups, reviews, messages, historicalAssertions, knownSubjects, caseId } = input;
  const bound: ClaimGroup[] = [];
  const authorized: SubjectRef[] = [];
  const diagnostics: { groupId: string; candidateId: string; status: 'verified' | 'normalized' | 'rejected'; reason: string }[] = [];
  const digest = (kind: string, ...parts: string[]) => `${kind}-${createHash('sha256').update(JSON.stringify([kind, ...parts])).digest('hex')}`;
  const units = new Set([...knownSubjects, ...historicalAssertions.filter(a => a.reviewStatus !== 'rejected').map(a => a.subjectRef)].filter(s => s.scope === 'buying_unit').map(s => s.id));
  for (const group of groups) {
    const scopes = new Set(group.candidates.map(c => c.subjectRef.scope));
    const matched = group.candidates.map(c => reviews.filter(r => r.groupId === group.groupId && r.candidateId === c.candidateId));
    const kinds = new Set(matched.flatMap(rs => rs.flatMap(r => r.subjectAttribution ? [r.subjectAttribution.kind] : [])));
    let rejected = scopes.size !== 1 || kinds.size > 1 || matched.some(rs => rs.length !== 1);
    const normalized = group.candidates.map((c, i) => {
      const review = matched[i][0]; const a = review?.subjectAttribution;
      const known = knownSubjects.some(s => s.scope === c.subjectRef.scope && s.id === c.subjectRef.id);
      const compatible = c.subjectRef.scope === 'case' ? 'case' : c.subjectRef.scope === 'buying_unit' ? 'buying_unit' : 'local_speaker';
      let subject: SubjectRef | undefined;
      // A known participant ID does not prove continuity in a different
      // message. The case itself is intrinsic; other references need S2.
      if (!a && known && ((c.subjectRef.scope === 'case' && c.subjectRef.id === caseId) || c.correction || !historicalAssertions.some(h => h.subjectRef.scope === c.subjectRef.scope && h.subjectRef.id === c.subjectRef.id))) subject = c.subjectRef;
      else if (a && a.kind === compatible && a.messageId === c.occurrence.messageId && review.atomicity === 'atomic' && review.support === 'supported' && a.justification.trim() && validateOccurrence(c.occurrence, messages)) {
        const message = messages.find(m => m.messageId === a.messageId);
        const span = c.occurrence.statementSpan;
        const valid = message?.content.type === 'text' && a.evidenceRefs.length > 0 && a.evidenceRefs.every(ref => {
          if (ref.messageId !== a.messageId || !ref.quote || message.content.type !== 'text') return false;
          const text = message.content.text; const start = ref.start ?? text.indexOf(ref.quote);
          const end = ref.end ?? start + ref.quote.length;
          return start >= span.start && end <= span.end && end > start && text.slice(start, end) === ref.quote && (ref.start !== undefined || text.indexOf(ref.quote, start + 1) < 0) && validateOccurrence({ messageId: a.messageId, statementSpan: span, focusSpan: { start, end, text: ref.quote } }, messages);
        });
        if (valid && !c.correction) {
          if (compatible === 'case') subject = { scope: 'case', id: caseId };
          if (compatible === 'local_speaker') subject = { scope: 'participant', id: digest('local', caseId, a.messageId) };
          if (compatible === 'buying_unit' && units.size <= 1) subject = { scope: 'buying_unit', id: digest('unit', caseId) };
          const history = historicalAssertions.filter(h => h.reviewStatus !== 'rejected' && h.fieldId === c.fieldId && sameEvidence(h.evidenceRefs, c.evidenceRefs, messages));
          if (history.length) {
            if (history.length === 1 && subject && history[0].subjectRef.scope === subject.scope && (subject.scope === 'case' || history[0].subjectRef.id === subject.id)) subject = history[0].subjectRef;
            else subject = undefined;
          }
          if (subject?.scope === 'buying_unit' && units.size && !units.has(subject.id)) subject = undefined;
        }
      }
      if (!subject) rejected = true;
      return { candidate: c, subject };
    });
    if (new Set(normalized.flatMap(x => x.subject ? [JSON.stringify(x.subject)] : [])).size > 1) rejected = true;
    for (const entry of normalized) diagnostics.push({ groupId: group.groupId, candidateId: entry.candidate.candidateId, status: rejected ? 'rejected' : JSON.stringify(entry.candidate.subjectRef) === JSON.stringify(entry.subject) ? 'verified' : 'normalized', reason: rejected ? 'Subject attribution requires review' : 'Subject attribution accepted' });
    if (rejected) continue;
    const candidates = normalized.map(({ candidate, subject }) => ({ ...candidate, subjectRef: subject! }));
    for (const c of candidates) if (!knownSubjects.some(s => s.scope === c.subjectRef.scope && s.id === c.subjectRef.id) && !authorized.some(s => s.scope === c.subjectRef.scope && s.id === c.subjectRef.id)) authorized.push(c.subjectRef);
    bound.push({ ...group, candidates });
  }
  return { status: diagnostics.some(d => d.status === 'rejected') ? 'human_review_required' as const : 'success' as const, groups: bound, authorizedSubjects: authorized, diagnostics };
}

/** Experimental, deliberately narrow grammar. This helper is not connected to
 * the pipeline: its input does not authenticate the message or resolve history. */
export function resolveLocalSubject(input: { caseId: string; messageId: string; text: string; scope: 'buying_unit' | 'participant'; focusStart: number; focusEnd: number }) {
  const { text, caseId, messageId, scope, focusStart, focusEnd } = input;
  const unresolved = { kind: 'unresolved' as const };
  if (!caseId || !messageId || focusStart < 0 || focusEnd <= focusStart || focusEnd > text.length) return unresolved;
  // Require the whole message to match a minimal, unquoted assertion. This is
  // intentionally not a general Spanish parser or a source-of-authority check.
  const amount = '(?:[0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?)';
  const single = new RegExp(`^yo gano\\s+${amount}(?:\\s+euros?)?\\s*[.!]?$`, 'iu');
  const buyer = new RegExp(`^compro yo solo y gano\\s+${amount}\\s*[.!]?$`, 'iu');
